Subject: Plug-in: a texture descriptor's swizzle is served, over its own memory and over an IOSurface

MTLTextureDescriptor.swizzle says how a texture is read: a one-channel mask
asked for as (R, R, R, 1), a surface's channels in another order. For a
texture of its own memory it was a refusal (nil, "only the identity is
served"); for one over an IOSurface the field was not looked at, and the
texture read its channels as they lie -- a one-channel picture as (r, 0, 0, 1).

Both are now made as before and then read through the swizzle
(-hakiosSwizzledBy:), the way a swizzled view already was: the same memory
through a descriptor of its own (hakios_metal_texture_new_swizzled), sampling
alone -- a store is not swizzled, in Metal either. The console says once that
a swizzle was asked for, and which.

In the core, a texture read through a swizzle keeps being memoryless when the
texture under it is.

No host test of the plug-in's half (it is not built on the host; compiled for
iOS). The core's swizzled textures have theirs; the one line added is checked
beside the memoryless test.


---
diff --git a/hakios-metal/src/texture.cpp b/hakios-metal/src/texture.cpp
index 7539430..6ea2e35 100644
--- a/hakios-metal/src/texture.cpp
+++ b/hakios-metal/src/texture.cpp
@@ -899,6 +899,7 @@ std::shared_ptr<Texture> Texture::swizzled(const std::shared_ptr<Texture>& textu
     std::shared_ptr<Texture> t = adopt(new Texture(p.buffer_, p.desc_, p.info_, p.pitch_, p.offset_, p.pitchAlign_, p.surface_));
     t->chroma_ = p.chroma_;
     t->layerPitch_ = p.layerPitch_;
+    t->memoryless_ = p.memoryless_;
     // over the parent's: a component naming red reads what the parent's red reads
     for (int c = 0; c < 4; c++) t->swizzle_[c] = swizzle[c] < 2 ? swizzle[c] : p.swizzle_[swizzle[c] - 2];
     return t;
